[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 8"""
 date="2026-09-03T15:23:08Z"
 content="""
I started writing docs for `remote.web.annex-gitcredentials`,
and quickly realized that it's confusing that, for a git remote,
`remote.<name>.annex-gitcredentials` is not needed in order for git-credential
to be used, while for a web special remote, it is needed.

That makes me wonder if the config is needed at all, or if it should
default to true. Either choice would mean that the security considerations
need to be considered again.

But: A git remote can also be set up to be autoenabled, with an attacker
controlled url. In that case, git-annex will already use the git credential
config when accessing files in that git remote, and so will git when
pulling from that remote.

So, there does not seem to be any additional security exposure in making the
web special remote use git-credential by default.
"""]]
